{title: We Three Kings of Orient Are}
{key: Em}
{time: 3/4}
{capo: 7}

We [Em]three kings of [B7]Orient [Em]are;
Bearing gifts we [B7]traverse a[Em]far,
Field and [D]fountain, [G]moor and [C]moun[Am]tain,
[Em]Following [B7]yonder [Em]star.

{label: Chorus}
[G]O star of wonder, [C]star of [G]night,
Star with royal [C]beauty [G]bright,
[Em]Westward [D]leading, [C]still pro[D]ceeding,
[G]Guide us to thy [C]perfect [G]light.

[Em]Born a King on [B7]Bethlehem's [Em]plain,
Gold I bring to [B7]crown Him a[Em]gain,
King for[D]ever, [G]ceasing [C]nev[Am]er,
[Em]Over us [B7]all to [Em]reign.

{label: Chorus}
[G]O star of wonder, [C]star of [G]night,
Star with royal [C]beauty [G]bright,
[Em]Westward [D]leading, [C]still pro[D]ceeding,
[G]Guide us to thy [C]perfect [G]light.

[Em]Glorious now be[B7]hold Him a[Em]rise,
King and God and [B7]sacri[Em]fice;
Alle[D]luia, [G]alle[C]lu[Am]ia,
[Em]Sounds through the [B7]earth and [Em]skies.

{label: Chorus}
[G]O star of wonder, [C]star of [G]night,
Star with royal [C]beauty [G]bright,
[Em]Westward [D]leading, [C]still pro[D]ceeding,
[G]Guide us to thy [C]perfect [G]light.
